{
  "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
  "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Joseph W. Jacquot",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "As courts have recognized, Miranda warnings protect Fifth Amendment rights and promote voluntary confessions, confessions important to seeking truth, solving crimes, and securing justice. Yet the Florida Supreme Court erred in two ways to suppress a voluntary confession relied upon for Kevin Powell's conviction."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0000-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The Florida Supreme Court could say: Well, that's very nice, but we have a Florida Constitution with a counterpart to the Fifth Amendment, so we're just going to have the same opinion, but we are putting it under -- squarely under the Florida Constitution. They could do that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0000",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Respondent's amici make the argument that it will somehow promote a race to the bottom."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0001",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 21,
        "start": 21
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "some police officers have attempted to evade Miranda by interrogation techniques, but there is no indication"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Aren't we encouraging that?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0003",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "this Court upheld the warning in Duckworth, which said, we have no way of providing you an attorney, but one will be provided if and when you go to court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0004",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "In fact, of the 900 warnings that are included in the survey that Respondent relies heavily on, only 5 have that formulation."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 23,
        "start": 23
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But your case has to be that, if we adopt the Petitioner's petition, it's perfectly fine for every jurisdiction in the country to use this warning, right?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0006",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We think that that concern is simply not warranted."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "You think lack of uniformity is a good idea?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "United States",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0008",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "four circuit courts have upheld general right to counsel warnings of the kind that were in the FBI warnings in 1966."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0011",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Isn't it wiser generally to have the same form used throughout the State?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0013",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Could you tell us where that is?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0001-0014",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The bottom line in my mind -- the question is, whether these warnings are substantively or otherwise different than the FBI warnings that some believe were approved in Miranda. Are these equivalent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0002-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 41,
        "start": 41
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Well, how about the reasonable defendant in this very case? Powell's lawyer questioned him and asked him: \"You waived the right to have an attorney present during your questioning by the detectives?\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Do you think that the average person hearing this warning would envision the sort of procedure that occurs before a grand jury?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Is there -- is there any -- I'm not sure this is pertinent -- but is there any malevolent reason Tampa police would adopt this warning? I mean, someone says, well, here's what the FBI uses."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. Brueckheimer",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRUECKHEIMER: It's -- it's hard for us to be able to delve into the minds of the Tampa Police Department and the people who create these forms."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Professor Leo",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0002-0004",
      "kind": "amicus_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 44,
        "start": 44
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. BRUECKHEIMER: Well, Professor Leo could, and there is a memo he attaches at the end of his appendix in the amicus brief, but I -- I would just say that it doesn't really matter what the motives are, and that it all depends on how the defendant or the person in custody is -- is perceiving these warnings and whether he's getting the information he or she needs to be --"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jacquot",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. JACQUOT: Mr. Chief Justice, let me make three brief points, after responding to a question that Justice Stevens asked."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Jacquot",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
      "evidence_id": "ev-44ccb8d7fe48-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 60,
        "start": 60
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There is no manipulation behind this warning. This warning is the result of litigation in Thompson v. State. That was a 1991 decision by the Florida Supreme Court."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2009-08-1175",
      "confidence": 0.0,
      "document_hash": "44ccb8d7fe48f56080ed7040b516a77c1402ec55ef11e5b433a0f1ed742ee127",
